If you haven't already created a virtual environment, you can create an conda env using the requirements.yaml file in this folder

> conda env create -f requirements.yaml

That should create an environment named "asdf-example".
Activate the environment before starting the notebook:

> conda activate asdf-example
> jupyter notebook


## If you haven't downloaded any example data
You can execute the grab_example_data.py script to download some examples

> python grab_example_data.py 

This script include STPSF data, you can comment out the download line if you dont want those.